  { q: "What do people traditionally eat or do on Qixi?", a: "Traditionally, people eat 'Qiaoguo' (巧果), a type of thin, fried pastry or sweet dough twist. Historically, women also engaged in 'Qiqiao' (pleading for skills) by threading needles in moonlight and carving melons to pray for dexterity in weaving and needlework." },
